From 5b27a3a51f459323789c78844e9225cd8717fd92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:37:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 174/274] DeepSeek V4.1 MoE: routed-expert scales as a row base
 and 4-bit codes

pack_scale_codes stores each output row's UE8M0 scales as its smallest
exponent and one 4-bit delta per scale, four to a 16-bit code per scale word,
and refuses a row spanning more than 16 exponents, so the codes are exact;
DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash's expert rows span at most 8. expand_scale_codes gives back
pack_scale_words' words byte for byte.

grouped_fp8_fp4_gemm(coded_scales=True) loads a stage's tile codes (tile_codes:
each tile's codes for one K block contiguous) in 16-byte copies and expands each
row's code into its scale word after the stage lands, before the barrier the MMA
already waits on: the same words, so the same output bits, from half the scale
bytes. The uncoded path allocates nothing new.

